# Columns & Cell Types

`columnProperties` maps each data key to a [`ComponentTypeProperties`](/api-reference/index/type-aliases/ComponentTypeProperties) entry that decides how the cell renders, sorts and exports. The `type` field is the only required key.

```typescript
import { ComponentType } from 'svelte-advanced-datatable';

const config: DataTableConfig<UserData> = {
    type: 'userData',
    columnProperties: {
        id:        { type: ComponentType.NUMBER },
        userName:  { type: ComponentType.STRING },
        active:    { type: ComponentType.BOOLEAN },
        lastLogin: { type: ComponentType.DATE },
        role:      {
            type: ComponentType.ENUM,
            values: ['admin', 'editor', 'viewer'],
            enumColorKey: { admin: 'error', editor: 'warning', viewer: 'info' }
        },
        avatar:    { type: ComponentType.CUSTOM, sortable: false, component: AvatarCell }
    },
    dataUniquePropertyKey: 'id'
};
```

## Shared properties (all types)

Every column inherits [`GenericComponentTypeProperties`](/api-reference/index/interfaces/GenericComponentTypeProperties):

| Property                  | Type                                            | Description                                                                                              | Default |
|:--------------------------|:------------------------------------------------|:---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|:--------|
| `sortable`                | `boolean`                                       | Header click sorts by this column. Disable for derived/custom cells.                                     | `true`  |
| `hidden`                  | `boolean`                                       | Hard-hide. Never rendered, never offered in the column-visibility list.                                  | `false` |
| `alwaysVisible`           | `boolean`                                       | Forces the column on; suppresses it from the visibility toggle list.                                     | `false` |
| `resizable`               | `boolean`                                       | Allow the user to drag the right edge of the header.                                                     | `true`  |
| `formatValue`             | `(value, item) => string`                       | Custom display formatter. Receives the cell value and the full row. Return a string.                     | —       |
| `formatValueEnableHtml`   | `boolean`                                       | Render `formatValue`'s return value as HTML. Beware XSS — the value is injected with `{@html}`.          | `false` |

## ComponentType.STRING / NUMBER

No extra properties — STRING renders as text, NUMBER as a right-aligned number. Use `formatValue` for currencies, units, etc.

```typescript
budget: {
    type: ComponentType.NUMBER,
    formatValue: (value) =>
        new Intl.NumberFormat(undefined, { style: 'currency', currency: 'USD' }).format(value as number)
}
```

## ComponentType.BOOLEAN

Renders a check/cross. Use when your data isn't a plain `true`/`false` (e.g. legacy `'Y'`/`'N'`).

| Property   | Type      | Description                                                                                  | Default |
|:-----------|:----------|:---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|:--------|
| `truthy`   | `unknown` | Value loosely compared against the cell. Anything else renders as false.                     | `true`  |
| `inverted` | `boolean` | Render the opposite of the resolved boolean.                                                 | `false` |

## ComponentType.ENUM

Coloured badge per value. Pair with `messageConfig.<key>.enumValue` to translate the visible labels.

| Property        | Type                                          | Description                                                                                        |
|:----------------|:----------------------------------------------|:---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| `values`        | `string[]`                                    | Every possible enum value. Sort order in the export header follows this.                            |
| `enumColorKey`  | `Partial<Record<Enum \| 'default' \| 'unknown', WrappedComponentColor \| string>>` | DaisyUI badge colours per value; `default` covers configured values without a colour, `unknown` covers values not in `values`. |

```typescript
gender: {
    type: ComponentType.ENUM,
    values: ['male', 'female'],
    enumColorKey: { male: 'info', female: 'error', default: 'primary', unknown: 'neutral' }
} satisfies EnumComponentTypeProperties<'male' | 'female'>
```

## ComponentType.DATE

Renders a luxon `DateTime` or a native `Date`. Override the formatter to localise.

| Property     | Type                          | Description                                                                  | Default                                  |
|:-------------|:------------------------------|:-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|:-----------------------------------------|
| `dateFormat` | `Intl.DateTimeFormatOptions`  | `Intl` formatter options passed to luxon. Equivalent to `DATETIME_MED` by default. | `{ year, month: 'short', day, hour, minute }` |

## ComponentType.CUSTOM

Mount your own component or snippet for full control. The component receives `{ key, value, item, colProps }` ([`CustomComponentProps`](/api-reference/index/interfaces/CustomComponentProps)).

```typescript
password: {
    type: ComponentType.CUSTOM,
    sortable: false,
    component: HiddenPasswordCellComponent
} satisfies CustomComponentTypeProperties<string>
```

The cell component (daisyUI flavour):

```svelte
<script lang="ts">
    import type { CustomComponentProps } from 'svelte-advanced-datatable';

    let { value }: CustomComponentProps<string> = $props();
    let isHidden = $state(true);

    function toggle(event: MouseEvent) {
        event.stopPropagation();
        isHidden = !isHidden;
    }
</script>

{#if isHidden}
    <button class='btn btn-error btn-xs' onclick={toggle}>Show</button>
{:else}
    <code class='bg-base-200 px-1 rounded' onclick={toggle}>{value}</code>
{/if}
```

**Always call `event.stopPropagation()` on interactive controls.** Without it the row's click handler (modal open / `onItemClick` / `buildItemUrl`) also fires.

Prefer `formatValue` over a custom component when all you need is a different display string — it's cheaper and keeps export output sensible. Use `snippet` (instead of `component`) when the cell needs closures over local state.

